{"task":{"id":"Prob149_ece241_2013_q4","spec":"
I would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following
interface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise
specified.

 - input  clk
 - input  reset
 - input  s (3 bits)
 - output fr2
 - output fr1
 - output fr0
 - output dfr

A large reservior of water serves several users. In order to keep the
level of water succificently high, three sensors are placed vertically at
5-inch intervals. When the water level is above the highest sensor s[2],
the input flow rate should be zero. When the level is below the lowest
sensor s[0], the flow rate should be at maximum (both Nominal flow valve
and Supplemental flow valve opened). The flow rate when the level is
between the upper and lower sensors is determined by two factors: the
water level and the level previous to the last sensor change. Each water
level has a nominal flow rate associated with it as show in the table
below. If the sensor change indicates that the previous level was lower
than the current level, the flow rate should be increased by opening the
Supplemental flow valve (controlled by dfr).

  Water Level           | Sensors Asserted | Nominal Flow Rate Inputs to be Asserted
  Above s[2]            | s[0], s[1], s[2] | None
  Between s[2] and s[1] | s[0], s[1]       | fr0
  Between s[1] and s[0] | s[0]             | fr0, fr1
  Below s[0]            | None             | fr0, fr1, fr2

Also include an active-high synchronous reset that resets the state
machine to a state equivalent to if the water level had been low for a
long time (no sensors asserted, and all four outputs asserted).

","interface":{"top":"TopModule","ports":[{"name":"clk","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"reset","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"s","direction":"input","width":3,"signed":false},{"name":"fr2","direction":"output","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"fr1","direction":"output","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"fr0","direction":"output","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"dfr","direction":"output","width":1,"signed":false}]},"constraints":"SystemVerilog, exactly one self-contained TopModule DUT. Inline all helper logic inside TopModule; do not define auxiliary modules. xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI."},"current":{"revision_id":"24d64b12-bc79-4370-ad06-5259d9d6de61","source_sha256":"44ea2bdad05fc936fedf15fc3b35332c2606d862ca17fc2cc489c318f9decf4b","source":"module TopModule (
    input  clk,
    input  reset,
    input  [2:0] s,
    output reg fr2,
    output reg fr1,
    output reg fr0,
    output reg dfr
);

    // Registered water level (0 = below s[0], 1 = between s[1] and s[0],
    // 2 = between s[2] and s[1], 3 = above s[2]).
    reg [1:0] state;
    reg [1:0] next;

    // Decode the sensor pattern into the current water level.
    always @(*) begin
        case (s)
            3'b000: next = 2'd0;
            3'b001: next = 2'd1;
            3'b011: next = 2'd2;
            3'b111: next = 2'd3;
            default: next = 2'd0;
        endcase
    end

    // Synchronous, active-high reset forces the "long time low" state.
    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (reset)
            state <= 2'd0;
        else
            state <= next;
    end

    // Outputs are a function of the registered level. The supplemental
    // valve (dfr) opens when the new level is higher than the stored level
    // (rising water) or always when at the lowest level.
    always @(*) begin
        fr2 = 1'b0;
        fr1 = 1'b0;
        fr0 = 1'b0;
        dfr = 1'b0;
        case (state)
            2'd0: begin
                fr2 = 1'b1;
                fr1 = 1'b1;
                fr0 = 1'b1;
                dfr = 1'b1;
            end
            2'd1: begin
                fr2 = 1'b0;
                fr1 = 1'b1;
                fr0 = 1'b1;
                dfr = (next > state);
            end
            2'd2: begin
                fr2 = 1'b0;
                fr1 = 1'b0;
                fr0 = 1'b1;
                dfr = (next > state);
            end
            default: begin
                fr2 = 1'b0;
                fr1 = 1'b0;
                fr0 = 1'b0;
                dfr = 1'b0;
            end
        endcase
    end

endmodule
"},"previous_tool_result":{"tool":"edit_dut","accepted":true,"observation":{"revision_id":"24d64b12-bc79-4370-ad06-5259d9d6de61","source_sha256":"44ea2bdad05fc936fedf15fc3b35332c2606d862ca17fc2cc489c318f9decf4b","verification_state":"UNVERIFIED","test_suite_id":"Prob149_ece241_2013_q4"}},"verification_key":null,"observed":null,"repair_control":{"mode":"normal","compacted":false,"best_revision_id":"d5c8c85a-2e88-43fb-901c-ef4580b56f40","best_source_sha256":"cd85756b62f6995d4b16c698a7f8e13fc8808465ac49f1239cd3e17336c75cb2","rejected":[{"revision_id":"a94ea9be-54a0-444f-89ed-59a32f534a64","source_sha256":"cbf68c0eec3d0fbafa1990e8f7572ce715c50cdea04c4168a2702bbe6422b530","reason":"NO_IMPROVEMENT","checks":2040,"mismatches":1194}]},"repair_ledger":[{"task_id":"Prob149_ece241_2013_q4","sample_id":"d80fdbed-07a9-4770-9029-698043daa991","variant_id":"C","revision_id":"d5c8c85a-2e88-43fb-901c-ef4580b56f40","source_sha256":"cd85756b62f6995d4b16c698a7f8e13fc8808465ac49f1239cd3e17336c75cb2","verification_key":"sha256:eaa8e340bc897f96c1a651b1f7ef006c5cad3c28fffb7cfc053eb10626a9cbb8","stage":"simulation","status":"FAIL","checks":2040,"mismatches":1194},{"task_id":"Prob149_ece241_2013_q4","sample_id":"d80fdbed-07a9-4770-9029-698043daa991","variant_id":"C","revision_id":"a94ea9be-54a0-444f-89ed-59a32f534a64","source_sha256":"cbf68c0eec3d0fbafa1990e8f7572ce715c50cdea04c4168a2702bbe6422b530","verification_key":"sha256:ae3daa83f57ccf2b1fb53ef2cb5b9ffa4ee412aa4c45fea092b1b9f5e7b1fa6e","stage":"simulation","status":"FAIL","checks":2040,"mismatches":1194}],"action_instruction":"Continue from the best verified observation. Rejected revisions were restored; try a different repair. Waveform samples are observations, not proven causes.","verification_state":"UNVERIFIED","history":[{"task_id":"Prob149_ece241_2013_q4","sample_id":"d80fdbed-07a9-4770-9029-698043daa991","variant_id":"C","revision_id":"d5c8c85a-2e88-43fb-901c-ef4580b56f40","source_sha256":"cd85756b62f6995d4b16c698a7f8e13fc8808465